## 3. Complete All Six Process Parameter Mappings

Configure the existing UDT members as follows:

| Existing UDT Parameter | UNICORN OPC Source | Expected Units |
|---|---|---|
| Conductivity | RunData/Cond | mS/cm |
| Pressure | RunData/System pressure | MPa |
| pH | RunData/pH | Dimensionless |
| Flow Rate | RunData/System flow | Convert ml/min to lpm |
| UV Absorbance | RunData/UV 1, 2 or 3 | mAU |
| Gradient | RunData/Conc B | % |

Use the actual discovered OPC NodeIds from the previous commissioning artifacts and current OPC address space.

Do not construct unverified NodeIds based solely on the names in this table.

Preserve the Default authentication context in the OPC item paths.

For UV Absorbance, use UV 1 as the provisional commissioning channel unless the customer parameter list or instrument configuration identifies another required channel.

Record this channel selection for customer confirmation.

For Gradient, use Conc B as the provisional commissioning source for buffer B concentration unless the customer requirements identify a different parameter.

Document any remaining semantic ambiguity as a SAT verification item.

## 4. Flow Rate Configuration

The existing Flow Rate member was previously identified as a memory tag.

Convert the existing member to an OPC source using an instance-level override.

Configure:

- valueSource = opc
- opcServer = Unicorn-2
- opcItemPath = verified System flow NodeId
- enabled = True

Preserve the existing Flow Rate tag name, data type, engineering units, hierarchy and SCADA bindings.

The UNICORN source reports flow in ml/min, while the existing SCADA uses lpm.

Implement the appropriate supported instance-level scaling:

Flow Rate (lpm) = System flow (ml/min) / 1000

Prefer Ignition's native OPC tag scaling functionality.

Verify scaling behavior, numerical precision, applicable range handling and data-quality propagation before deployment.

Do not introduce a scaling configuration that clips valid readings.

Do not modify the parent UDT or existing graphical bindings.

If native scaling cannot implement the conversion correctly, document the specific limitation and minimum supported alternative.

