## 7. Data Quality Assessment

The previous commission established that the existing application may interpret Good_NoData as Good.

Investigate the minimum supported instance-level mechanism for propagating unavailable measurement quality correctly while keeping the process tags and KeyCPP references enabled.

Preserve the raw OPC status information.

Good_NoData and known initialization placeholders shall not be represented as verified physical measurements.

If the existing configuration cannot safely distinguish unavailable data:

- Retain the permanent OPC mappings and enabled acquisition tags.
- Document the quality discrimination deficiency.
- Use an existing supported commissioning or unavailable-data indication if available.
- Restrict affected graphical displays from normal operator reliance until corrected.
- Do not silently present placeholder measurements as valid.
- Provide a separate minimum-change proposal for correcting quality discrimination if necessary.

Do not modify parent UDT definitions or SCADA bindings without separate authorization.

Do not force data quality to Good.

Do not disable OPC acquisition as a workaround for instrument unavailability.

